---
import CodeTabs from '../../components/CodeTabs.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Authentication">
  <div class="callout" role="note">
    <svg class="callout-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
      <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
      <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
    </svg>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <strong>API keys are not being issued right now.</strong>
      Each cache miss hits a paid upstream provider, so issuing keys broadly isn't sustainable at the moment.
      Cached responses cover the vast majority of songs and need no key. If you hit a song that isn't cached,
      see <a href="#loading-uncached-songs">Loading uncached songs</a> below for a workaround.
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The Better Lyrics API uses a <strong>cache-first authentication model</strong>.
    Anyone can read a cached response. A fresh fetch may need an API key.
  </p>

  <h2>When you need an API key</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Scenario</th>
        <th>API key required?</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Cache hit (lyrics already cached)</td>
        <td>No</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cache miss (fresh fetch needed)</td>
        <td>Yes*</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Revalidation (<code>/revalidate</code> endpoint)</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Rate limit bypass</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note">*Only on <code>/getLyrics</code> and <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code>, and only when <code>API_KEY_REQUIRED</code> is enabled on the server. <code>/kugou/getLyrics</code> and <code>/qq/getLyrics</code> never need a key. Keys are currently not being issued to new users.</p>

  <h2>Using your API key</h2>
  <p>Pass your API key in the <code>X-API-Key</code> header:</p>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl -H "X-API-Key: your-api-key" \\
  "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154", {
  headers: { "X-API-Key": "your-api-key" },
});
const data = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get(
    "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154",
    headers={"X-API-Key": "your-api-key"},
)
data = res.json()` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	req, err := http.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154", nil)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	req.Header.Set("X-API-Key", "your-api-key")

	res, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />

  <h2>API key benefits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Fetch lyrics for songs that are not in the cache yet</li>
    <li>Skip rate limiting entirely</li>
    <li>Force a refresh of cached lyrics with the <code>/revalidate</code> endpoint</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Response headers</h2>
  <p>The API reports authentication state in these headers:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Header</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-Auth-Mode</code></td>
        <td>
          Current auth mode: <code>authenticated</code> (valid API key), <code>invalid</code> (invalid API key provided), or
          <code>cache</code> (no API key, so only cached lyrics are served). Sent only on JSON responses from <code>/getLyrics</code>,
          <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code> and <code>/revalidate</code>, and only when the server enforces API keys.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Bypass</code></td>
        <td>Set to <code>true</code> on every response when rate limits are bypassed via API key</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Error responses</h2>

  <h3>Missing API key (cache miss)</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "API key required",
  "message": "Uncached queries require a valid API key via X-API-Key header"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>Status: <code>401 Unauthorized</code></p>

  <h3>Invalid API key</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Invalid API key",
  "message": "The provided API key is not valid"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>Status: <code>401 Unauthorized</code></p>

  <h2 id="loading-uncached-songs">Loading uncached songs</h2>
  <p>
    First check that your request sends all four parameters: the cache key includes album and duration,
    so a request without them often misses an entry that is already cached. If a song you need still isn't
    cached, play it once with the
    <a href="https://better-lyrics.boidu.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Better Lyrics</a>
    extension installed. The extension fetches lyrics through the same upstream
    the API uses, so after that one playback the response is cached and any
    caller can get it without a key.
  </p>
  <p>
    This only works if the song exists upstream. If the extension can't find it
    either, playing it again won't help.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have the lyrics yourself, you can upload them directly at
    <a href="https://unison.boidu.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">unison.boidu.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cache-first model explained</h2>
  <p>
    Each request goes through these steps:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Request comes in for lyrics</li>
    <li>API checks if lyrics are already cached</li>
    <li>If cached: return immediately (no API key needed)</li>
    <li>If not cached: check for valid API key</li>
    <li>With valid API key: fetch from source, cache, and return</li>
    <li>Without API key: return 401 error</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    So anyone can read a song that is already cached. Only fresh fetches, which
    cost an upstream request, need a key.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
